543 :     }
```

Current bug report: {'summary': 'LocaleUtils.toLocale does not parse strings starting with an underscore', 'description': 'Hi,\nJavadocs of Locale.toString() states that "If the language is missing, the string will begin with an underbar.". This is not handled in the LocaleUtils.toLocale method if it is meant to be the inversion method of Locale.toString().\nThe fix for the ticket 328 does not handle well the case "fr\\_\\_P", which I found out during fixing the first bug.\nI am attaching the patch for both problems.\n'}

Recent bug reports (SBERT retrieval results with similarity): [{'similarity': 0.3, 'summary': 'Improve StringUtils.is(Not)Blank with a CharSequence... version', 'description': "Currently it's only possible to compare a single CharSequence per is(Not)Blank/is(Not)Empty call. This should be changed to support multiple CharSequences in a single call. ```\nif(StringUtils.isNotBlank(foo) && StringUtils.isNotBlank(bar) && ...)\n```"}, {'similarity': 0.36, 'summary': 'StringIndexOutOfBoundsException in CharSequenceTranslator', 'description': 'I found that there is bad surrogate pair handling in the CharSequenceTranslator\nThis is a simple test case for this problem. \\uD83D\\uDE30 is a surrogate pair. ```\n@Test\npublic void testEscapeSurrogatePairs() throws Exception {\n    assertEquals("\\uD83D\\uDE30", StringEscapeUtils.escapeCsv("\\uD83D\\uDE30"));\n}\n```'}, {'similarity': 0.16, 'summary': 'StringUtils join APIs for primitives', 'description': 'StringUtils join for primitives. Specifically, I need join(long[], char)\nBut might as well add APIs for all primitive types.'}]

